"""Durable, model-independent state for managed lane participants.

This module owns the small controller state machine used by the managed lane
supervisor.  It deliberately does not know how to start Claude, switch
profiles, or speak the SDK.  A state store is an injected boundary (the real
``ManagedStateStore`` and tiny in-memory fakes both work), while a runtime is
used only after a mailbox dispatch-intent has been durably recorded.

The controller methods are synchronous except for :meth:`dispatch_next`.
That method performs the potentially asynchronous runtime send *after* the
state write and never keeps a state-store lock across the send or its await.
"""

